{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation","id":1386055,"title":"Magical Treasures From Beyond Creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-06T07:02:39-07:00","id":1386055,"title":"Magical Treasures From Beyond Creation","content":"<span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">So, </span></span></span><i>hypothetically speaking,</i><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> suppose that there is a larger Multiverse outside Creation. And suppose that there are conspiracies and cabals at work across the chain of worlds that have, for their own private reasons, decided to meddle in the Fate of Creation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Now, such cabals would normally be at a great disadvantage when contending against the Chosen, but such cabals might also have one great advantage: access to the treasures and wonders of a thousand worlds. So, what strange and evocative artifacts and wonders might such cabals utilise? Ioun stones? IOUN stones, even? Excaliber? Stormbringer? Morganti blades by the dozen?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T09:08:52-07:00","id":1386096,"title":"","content":"By definition, anything beyond the borders of Creation is Wyld and Fae, even if only a small portion of the Fae are Raksha.<br /> <br /> So you're talking about Fae treasures, and we don't have clear guidelines for those yet, but in past Editions, the Raksha could indeed forge powerful treasures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T09:21:02-07:00","id":1386100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386096#post1386096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By definition, anything beyond the borders of Creation is Wyld and Fae, even if only a small portion of the Fae are Raksha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Zen-Mu &quot;Wyld and Fae?&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bFor that matter, Malfeas and Autochthonia both exist beyond the borders of Creation, and <i>neither of those</i> is Wyld.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere could well exist other worlds outside the boundaries of Creation, worlds that exist <i>in</i> the Wyld, yet are not <i>of</i> the Wyld.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot sure how we ended up with Ioun stones though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T09:32:13-07:00","id":1386103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386100#post1386100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNot sure how we ended up with Ioun stones though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thread seems to suggest bringing items from other existing fantasy universes.<br /> <br /> In which case I'll take the Helm of Governance and a Ring of Three Wishes from Golarion, should be off to a good start with that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:23:28-07:00","id":1386109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386096#post1386096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By definition, anything beyond the borders of Creation is Wyld and Fae, even if only a small portion of the Fae are Raksha.<br /> <br /> So you're talking about Fae treasures, and we don't have clear guidelines for those yet, but in past Editions, the Raksha could indeed forge powerful treasures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naah, we have Zen-Mu, hypothetical worlds of Yatani's Children, &quot;yet stranger places&quot; from Arms of the Chosen, explictly different from &quot;Chaos beyond the World&quot; (I quote from memory). And this is just sticking to 3e canon. There clearly is some, very hypothetical and wide open, room for a Multiverse.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, I see. I didn't know what Ioun stone is. Excalibur is an interesting thought exercise though, since on one hand it's very distant thematically from Exalted and on the other Creation at least used to be the prehistory of WoD and Ars Magica had unclearish links to Mage and there is some link from Ars Magica to Arthurian legends, so I could see a basis for some very gonzo comic-book Multiverse crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 05-07-2020, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:30:57-07:00","id":1386111,"title":"","content":"So uh ...<br /> <br /> I rolled 46 on Table C. It's a potion of Frost Giant Strength. <br /> <br /> Hope that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T16:29:18-07:00","id":1386203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386100#post1386100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Zen-Mu &quot;Wyld and Fae?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Primordials made Zen-Mu, so it's an exception.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bFor that matter, Malfeas and Autochthonia both exist beyond the borders of Creation, and <i>neither of those</i> is Wyld. </div> </div> </div>They're both Primordials, and Primordials are something that can emerge from the Wyld like Raksha.<br /> <br /> They just happen to be superior than Raksha at insisting that they matter, and making things (like Creation) to enforce that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T18:06:15-07:00","id":1386219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386203#post1386203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Primordials made Zen-Mu, so it's an exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>And who's to say Zen-Mu and Creation are the only worlds made by Primordials? (We already know of at least one other world that was made by a singular Primordial in 2e, though it was destroyed.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386203#post1386203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're both Primordials, and Primordials are something that can emerge from the Wyld like Raksha.<br /> <br /> They just happen to be superior than Raksha at insisting that they matter, and making things (like Creation) to enforce that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And who's to say that Primordials are the only non-fae - or even the first non-fae - to do that?<br /> <br /> \u200bAs <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13416_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13416\" data-vbnamecard=\"13416\">Lanic</a> said earlier, we've already got Yatani's Children. Are <i>they</i> Wyld and/or Fae?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-06-2020, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T00:16:21-07:00","id":1386296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386219#post1386219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAs <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13416_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13416\" data-vbnamecard=\"13416\">Lanic</a> said earlier, we've already got Yatani's Children. Are <i>they</i> Wyld and/or Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, the way Yatani's Children are presented, it may well happen that they are completely wrong about their world.<br /> <br /> I must admit that I'm very fond of the way Exalted 3 handles &quot;multiverse&quot; It leaves just enough hints that a Storyteller can feel justified in introducing otherwordly plots (of which I'm an enthusiast), but makes information just scarce enough that it does not simply amount to inflating the map.<br /> <br /> I'm especially thinking of &quot; places that the Second Age has no name for or language to describe.&quot; There probably are other places, but we leave it up to you, since they are, you know, <i>other</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T00:18:15-07:00","id":1386298,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Posted by mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T00:35:12-07:00","id":1386301,"title":"","content":"Very true, and I feel it is a good direction; however, the bone of my contention was not whether there must factually be other worlds beyond Creation, but whether those other worlds <i>must</i> be of the Wyld (at least, moreso than Creation itself is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-07-2020, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T13:51:25-07:00","id":1386477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386301#post1386301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very true, and I feel it is a good direction; however, the bone of my contention was not whether there must factually be other worlds beyond Creation, but whether those other worlds <i>must</i> be of the Wyld (at least, moreso than Creation itself is).</div> </div> </div> </div>To answer that, first one must ask, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me\">&quot;What <i>is</i> the Wyld&quot;?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:38:34-07:00","id":1386498,"title":"","content":"Stormbringer is Soulfarer but a sword. I\u2019m unfamiliar with the original IOUN stones or these Morganti blades. Excalibur in...what medium? It\u2019s a 5 dot artifact probably, but I know at least one anime has it destroying an entire alien fleet or soemthing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:51:39-07:00","id":1386503,"title":"","content":"Would Master Materia be useful for this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:31:24-07:00","id":1386539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386477#post1386477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To answer that, first one must ask, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me\">&quot;What <i>is</i> the Wyld&quot;?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The Core book seems to have a pretty decent answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Ex3 Core Book, p. 30</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wyld, the:</b> Chaos and entropy, the infinite precursor to reality. <i>Creation</i> was raised up from the Wyld, and the Wyld was bound and subsumed into its substance. The Wyld still exists beyond the borders of the world, pressing inward and ever threatening to dissolve the lands of shape back into shifting unreality. Strange lands and strange things dwell within and emerge from the Wyld, including the <i>Fair Folk</i>. Pockets of the Wyld exist in Creation\u2019s interior, remnants of the Fair Folk\u2019s invasion long ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere are strange lands located within the Wyld, but considering that the Wyld can exist inside Creation's interior, I still see no reason why those lands <i>must</i> be considered &quot;the Wyld&quot; if Creation (a land <i>entirely surrounded by, and even containing some of</i> the Wyld) gets a pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T18:27:32-07:00","id":1386580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386539#post1386539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThere are strange lands located within the Wyld, but considering that the Wyld can exist inside Creation's interior, I still see no reason why those lands <i>must</i> be considered &quot;the Wyld&quot; if Creation (a land <i>entirely surrounded by, and even containing some of</i> the Wyld) gets a pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you suggesting that somewhere in the Wyld, a Primordial made their own Creation?<br /> <br /> Or maybe a powerful creature as different from Primordials as Primordials are from the Raksha?<br /> <br /> That just as the Wyld gave rise to the Primordials, the Wyld can produce any number of creatures which are not Raksha?<br /> <br /> The common fae themselves are, last I checked, millions of different kinds of creatures enslaved by the Raksha. All of them similar enough to each other to be called &quot;fae&quot;, but the Raksha being something inherently more powerful; strong enough to enslave all of the others.<br /> <br /> Does the Wyld still produce Raksha, or did it produce them only once, and the Raksha proved strong enough to perpetuate themselves in spite of the Wyld's dangers, including pre-existing competitors and new challengers?<br /> <br /> The Wyld clearly seemed to produce the Primordials only once, and while they aren't in the business of making more of themselves, they did prove powerful enough to survive and conquer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T19:00:01-07:00","id":1386589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386580#post1386580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you suggesting that somewhere in the Wyld, a Primordial made their own Creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019ve done it before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386580#post1386580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe a powerful creature as different from Primordials as Primordials are from the Raksha?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m suggesting that you don\u2019t categorically rule it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386580#post1386580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just as the Wyld gave rise to the Primordials, the Wyld can produce any number of creatures which are not Raksha?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386580#post1386580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The common fae themselves are, last I checked, millions of different kinds of creatures enslaved by the Raksha.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is a \u201ckind?\u201d<br /> <br /> To whit, if all that comes from the Wyld are the creators, the Raksha, and the slaves of the Raksha, would that not mean there are <i>three</i> kinds of creatures native to the Wyld?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386580#post1386580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of them similar enough to each other to be called &quot;fae&quot;, but the Raksha being something inherently more powerful; strong enough to enslave all of the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely we don\u2019t <b>know</b> that <i>all</i> the things of the Wyld are the playthings of raksha. Are the zouaves of the Scorpion Empire slaves of the Fair Folk?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386580#post1386580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Wyld still produce Raksha, or did it produce them only once, and the Raksha proved strong enough to perpetuate themselves in spite of the Wyld's dangers, including pre-existing competitors and new challengers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question! I don\u2019t think either of us knows the answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386580#post1386580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyld clearly seemed to produce the Primordials only once, and while they aren't in the business of making more of themselves, they did prove powerful enough to survive and conquer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe, just spitballing here, considering the creators themselves journeyed across the Wyld for countless aeons to find the rock upon which Creation would be built, is it not possible the Wyld has since birthed more, but they haven\u2019t journeyed this way yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-08-2020, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T11:42:48-07:00","id":1386748,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, I\u2019d say it\u2019s more useful to assume that the Wyld could have anything you want in it, including other stable realities (or at least portals to other stable realities), than to assume that it axiomatically can\u2019t.<br /> <br /> As for bringing magical items from outside the game inside, my advice would be to use what you like as inspiration for building your own artifacts. Arms of the Chosen has a Not!Stormbringer and a Not!Eva in it, so you can probably have Ioun Stones if you want (though a blanket +1 to a stat is both boring and potentially game breaking, so you might need to tweak the effects a bit, but an artifact that\u2019s a gemstone that floats around your head seems like it\u2019s entirely doable)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:01:27-07:00","id":1386821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386748#post1386748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking, I\u2019d say it\u2019s more useful to assume that the Wyld could have anything you want in it, including other stable realities (or at least portals to other stable realities), than to assume that it axiomatically can\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but that doesn't mean anything born to those realities can exist inside Creation's reality.<br /> <br /> The behemoth trapped in the moonsilver warstrider was such a creature. A behemoth of Zen-Mu, its reality was incompatible with Creation's, and it was strong enough that it imposed its reality over Creation's, obliterating all Creation it touched. It couldn't even PERCEIVE Creation; it was just blindly taking a stroll that happened to put it on an intercept course with the Loom of Fate before a Lunar and his Terrestrial followers managed to pin it down and contain it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for bringing magical items from outside the game inside, my advice would be to use what you like as inspiration for building your own artifacts. Arms of the Chosen has a Not!Stormbringer and a Not!Eva in it, so you can probably have Ioun Stones if you want (though a blanket +1 to a stat is both boring and potentially game breaking, so you might need to tweak the effects a bit, but an artifact that\u2019s a gemstone that floats around your head seems like it\u2019s entirely doable) </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> The most interesting thing about other Creations in the Wyld would be the other Creations, not the artifacts made within them. The people of Creation can make any of their own artifacts as they please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}